KDE Infinite Desktop for Debian / Ubuntu / KDE neon
==================================================

This directory lives in packaging/debian/ of the upstream sources. Build with

  ./build.sh --package            (puts the .deb files into ./dist/)

or by hand:

  cp -r packaging/debian debian
  chmod 0755 debian/rules         # other files in debian/ must not be executable
  sudo apt build-dep ./           # or: mk-build-deps -ir
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The effect needs KWin >= 6.8 (KDE neon today; Debian/Ubuntu once they ship
Plasma 6.8). Without it only the settings app and the data can be built:

  DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=pkg.kde-infinite-desktop.noeffect dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

KWin only loads plugins built for exactly its version. kwin-effect-infinitedesktop
therefore depends on the upstream KWin version it was built against
(kwin-wayland >= X.Y.Z, << X.Y.Z.1~). After a KWin update apt keeps the KWin
update back until a matching rebuild is installed (a repository that rebuilds
automatically, e.g. the openSUSE Build Service, does that for you). The
from-source installer scripts/install.sh rebuilds automatically instead.
